xnu 0426: every Apple80211 SET is said in the log

The request log stops after 800 lines, and wifid's reads (SCAN_RESULT, CURRENT_NETWORK: hundreds a minute with
Settings open) used them up before a join was tried from Settings. On 2026-11-20 a join from Settings failed at once
with -3903 (kCWNotSupportedErr, the driver's EOPNOTSUPP), while wifijoin's lone ASSOCIATE joins the same network: the
SET that wifid makes and the driver does not answer went unlogged. Reads keep the 800-line limit; every SET is logged.
---
diff --git a/bsd/dev/sapphire_apple80211.c b/bsd/dev/sapphire_apple80211.c
index d660bb6..10eb8c7 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sapphire_apple80211.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sapphire_apple80211.c
@@ -856,9 +856,13 @@ sapphire_apple80211_ioctl(u_long command, void *data)
 	proc_selfname(who, sizeof(who));
 	error = is_set ? set(request, what, sizeof(what)) : get(request, what, sizeof(what));
 	note(request, is_set, error);
-	/* (a request that is repeated for ever is said a few hundred times) */
-	if (said < 800 || request->req_type == 51) {        /* (0424: the country, always) */
-		said++;
+	/*
+	 * (a request that is repeated for ever is said a few hundred times). 0426: every SET is said: wifid's reads of the
+	 * scan results and the current network (hundreds a minute) used the 800 lines up before a join from Settings, and
+	 * which request wifid made of a join, and what it was told, went unsaid.
+	 */
+	if (said < 800 || is_set || request->req_type == 51) {        /* (0424: the country, always) */
+		said += is_set ? 0 : 1;
 		printf("apple80211: %s %s %d (%s), value %d, %u bytes%s: %s", who, is_set ? "sets" : "gets", request->req_type,
 		    type_name(request->req_type), request->req_val, request->req_len, what, error == 0 ? "answered\n" : error ==
 		    EOPNOTSUPP ? "REFUSED\n" : "");
